  "text": "We are given the recursive definition of a sequence of polynomials $ P_n(x) $:\n\n- $ P_1(x) = 1 - x $\n- $ P_n(x) = P_{n-1}(x) \\cdot (1 - x^{2n-1}) $, for $ n \\geq 2 $\n\nOur goal is to show that for any positive integer $ n $, the polynomial $ P_n(x) $ satisfies:\n\n> **If we multiply it out and discard all terms involving $ x $ to a power larger than $ n^2 $, the result is just $ 1 - x $.**\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Base Case**\n\nLet’s check the base case $ n = 1 $.\n\n- $ P_1(x) = 1 - x $\n\n- Multiply it out and discard all terms larger than $ 1^2 = 1 $, so only the term $ 1 - x $ is left.\n\n✅ **Base case holds.**\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Inductive Hypothesis**\n\nAssume that for some positive integer $ n $, the polynomial $ P_n(x) $ satisfies the condition:\n\n> $ P_n(x) = 1 - x $, after multiplying out and discarding all terms of degree greater than $ n^2 $.\n\nThat is, we can write:\n\n$$\nP_n(x) = 1 - x + \\text{terms with } x^k \\text{ for } k \\leq n^2\n$$\n\nWe are told that:\n\n$$\nP_n(x) = 1 - x \\quad \\text{(after discarding higher degree terms)}\n$$\n\nSo, the assumption is that:\n\n$$\nP_n(x) = 1 - x\n$$\n\nWe now need to show that this holds for $ P_{n+1}(x) $.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Use of the Recursive Formula**\n\nWe use the recursive definition:\n\n$$\nP_n(x) = P_{n-1}(x) \\cdot (1 - x^{2n-1})\n$$\n\nLet’s compute $ P_{n+1}(x) $:\n\n$$\nP_{n+1}(x) = P_n(x) \\cdot (1 - x^{2n+1})\n$$\n\nSubstitute $ P_n(x) = 1 - x $:\n\n$$\nP_{n+1}(x) = (1 - x) \\cdot (1 - x^{2n+1})\n$$\n\nNow expand this:\n\n$$\n(1 - x)(1 - x^{2n+1}) = 1 \\cdot (1 - x^{2n+1}) - x(1 - x^{2n+1})\n$$\n\n$$\n= 1 - x^{2n+1} - x + x^{2n+2}\n$$\n\nNow, collect terms:\n\n- The term $ x^{2n+2} $ is of degree $ 2n + 2 $, which is **greater than** $ n^2 = (2n+1)^2 = 4n^2 + 4n + 1 $, so it is **discarded**.\n- The remaining terms are:\n\n$$\n1 - x - x^{2n+1}\n$$\n\nBut since we are **only** interested in terms up to degree $ n^2 $, we discard $ x^{2n+1} $, and so:\n\n$$\nP_{n+1}(x) = 1 - x\n$$\n\n✅ **Inductive step holds.**\n\n---\n\n### ✅ **Final Answer:**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{1 - x}\n$$",
